				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/agentwilson" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(802114); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=802114&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606273926" alt="AgentWilson" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=802114)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/agentwilson" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(802114); return false;" >AgentWilson</a></span> <span class="odate time_1526480539 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">16 May 2018 14:22</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3802284">
									

<p>Agreed. The &quot;box&quot; does not necessarily mean a literal box (as in a locker, containment cell, etc.) The &quot;box&quot; is the containment procedure, and as long as the &quot;box&quot; isn't too fiddly, it's Safe. Feeding and cleaning up after them is part of the &quot;box&quot;. They aren't a separate procedure needed to keep the &quot;box&quot; working effectively.</p>
<p>This one's &quot;box&quot; is literally &quot;leave it in an enclosed orchard&quot; and &quot;feed it anything hazardous or compostable.&quot;</p>
<p>According to the style guidelines:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>any SCP that's autonomous, sentient and/or sapient is generally classified as Euclid, due to the inherent unpredictability of an object that can act or think on its own.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>However, I am inclined to say this could be classified as Safe. Despite being intelligent, it doesn't want to escape. It perfectly happy where it is.</p>

							</div>

								
					
