					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/fieldstone" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1436137); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1436137&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606273926" alt="fieldstone" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1436137)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/fieldstone" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1436137); return false;" >fieldstone</a></span> <span class="odate time_1526482084 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">16 May 2018 14:48</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3802303">
									

<p>I see the logic here - you could define &quot;box&quot; a number of ways - but an enclosed orchard would require maintenance (even if the thing takes care of the plants itself, you'd need someone to keep an eye on it to make sure that stays stable) and eventual repairs for whatever irrigation system you have in there. Feeding it waste would require someone to gather and deliver the waste.</p>
<p>Even though it doesn't want to escape, it seems pretty sociable, and there's no reason to think it would react to solitary confinement any better than any other intelligent being does. So you would need to provide it with companions and probably the occasional evaluation to make sure that its mental condition is stable. Since its body seems to be composed of a pretty complex ecosystem, you would probably also want some kind of veterinarian or zoologist to take a look at him from time to time.</p>
<p>So now we've got a botanist, a couple different kinds of engineer, a zoologist, maintenance workers, and counselors all involved in the containment of this thing. Those personnel need to be scheduled, managed, transported etc. This is a box that would require a good deal of ongoing intervention to maintain, which is the definition of Euclid. It's not just about the difficulty of preventing a breach, it's about the difficulty of keeping the thing secure and protected in addition to containing it.</p>

							</div>

								
					
